knowledge:
- key_parameters:
    - s.len=The number of threshold values to test (default is 100; can be set lower, e.g., 25, to reduce computation time). ;;
    - s.min=The minimum threshold value to test. ;;
    - s.max=The maximum threshold value to test. ;;
    - normalization=The normalization strategy to use prior to filtering (e.g., "TMM", "DESeq", "pseudo.counts", or "none"). ;;
    - plot=Logical indicating whether to plot the global Jaccard index (default is TRUE). ;;
    - DGEList=The DGEList object containing library sizes and normalization factors, required when filtering DGEExact objects. ;;
    - DGEGLM=The DGEGLM object (fit), required when filtering DGELRT objects.
- alternatives:
    - DESeq2 independent filtering=DESeq2's default independent filtering procedure in the results() function is an alternative targeting the same weakly expressed genes. If using HTSFilter, set independentFiltering=FALSE in the DESeq2 results() function. ;;
    - genefilter=A Bioconductor package designed for independent filtering of microarray data rather than RNA-seq data.
- when_to_use:
    - Use when performing gene-level differential expression analyses on replicated RNA-seq (or other count-based transcriptome sequencing) data. It is appropriate when biological replicates are present for each experimental condition and the data can be normalized to correct for systematic inter-sample biases.
- pitfalls:
    - Do not apply HTSFilter to data that has already been filtered, as this will result in a plateau of Jaccard index values and filter no genes. ;;
    - Although the filter can be applied earlier in the edgeR pipeline (to DGEList or DGEGLM objects), it is not recommended because parameter estimation in edgeR makes use of pseudo-counts. Apply it to DGEExact or DGELRT objects instead. ;;
    - When using HTSFilter within the DESeq2 pipeline, you must set independentFiltering=FALSE in the results() function to prevent DESeq2 from applying its own redundant filter.
